8a6e3d8 test(orchestrator): fix prompt builder config and single-expect rule
Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>


 specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md              |  2 +-
 ...atOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts | 25 ++++++++++------------
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)
=== diff ===
commit 8a6e3d8ce9644480f2cf04502b9ffcc1146bfc09
Author: loop-bench <loop-bench@localhost>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 17:54:50 2026 +0100

    test(orchestrator): fix prompt builder config and single-expect rule

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md b/specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md
index 77b9e69..59dec9e 100644
--- a/specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md
+++ b/specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
 - A `beforeModelResponse` hook installed through config is handed the base system prompt built from `prompt`, proving the hook reaches the orchestrator and is wired into the prompt pipeline rather than only being stored on the config ([validated by: hands a config-installed beforeModelResponse hook the built base system prompt, not merely storing it](../../src/config.test.ts#L108)).
 - The value the hook returns then replaces the system prompt the provider receives; this is exercised at the orchestrator layer because `HalEngineConfig.provider` takes a `ProviderConfig` and offers no seam to inject a recording provider through config ([validated by: replaces system prompt with returned value](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L216)).
 - For a session that completes without error the hooks fire in the order `beforeSession` → `beforeUserInput` → `afterUserInput` → `beforeModelResponse` → `afterModelResponse` → `afterSession` ([validated by: fires the lifecycle hooks in documented order for a session that completes without error](../../src/config.test.ts#L132)).
-- `beforeSession` runs inside the turn's `try` block, so a throw there reaches the `catch` and `finally` blocks and fires both `onError` and `afterSession` before the rejection reaches the caller; because the throw aborts the turn before `beforeUserInput`, `beforeModelResponse`, any provider call or any tool round runs, `afterSession` cannot assume `beforeSession` finished allocating and must guard its release logic when releasing something `beforeSession` may have failed partway through allocating ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40), [validated by: runs onError then afterSession and skips the turn when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L116)).
+- `beforeSession` runs inside the turn's `try` block, so a throw there reaches the `catch` and `finally` blocks and fires both `onError` and `afterSession` before the rejection reaches the caller; because the throw aborts the turn before `beforeUserInput`, `beforeModelResponse`, any provider call or any tool round runs, `afterSession` cannot assume `beforeSession` finished allocating and must guard its release logic when releasing something `beforeSession` may have failed partway through allocating ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L36), [validated by: runs onError then afterSession and skips the turn when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L116)).

 ## Engine startup

diff --git a/src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts b/src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts
index 7c4797f..66c4d90 100644
--- a/src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts
+++ b/src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts
@@ -26,15 +26,11 @@ function createMockProvider(response: string): AIProvider {
   };
 }

-const promptBuilder = new PromptBuilder({
-  baseSystemPrompt: 'You are HAL.',
-  systemPromptSuffix: 'Be precise.',
-  contextConfig: {
-    historyLength: 10,
-    includeTimestamps: false,
-    includeSystemPrompt: true,
-  },
-});
+const promptBuilder = new PromptBuilder({identity: 'You are HAL.'});
+
+// One expect per test needs the rejection as a value rather than a matcher.
+const outcomeOf = (call: Promise<unknown>): Promise<string> =>
+  call.then(() => 'resolved without throwing').catch((error: Error) => error.message);

 describe('beforeSession throwing', () => {
   it('runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws', async () => {
@@ -57,11 +53,12 @@ describe('beforeSession throwing', () => {
       },
     });

-    await expect(orchestrator.processMessage(createSession('hello'))).rejects.toThrow(
-      'Database connection failed in beforeSession'
-    );
+    const outcome = await outcomeOf(orchestrator.processMessage(createSession('hello')));

-    expect(caughtError).toBe(errorToThrow);
-    expect(afterSessionRan).toBe(true);
+    expect({outcome, caughtError, afterSessionRan}).toEqual({
+      outcome: 'Database connection failed in beforeSession',
+      caughtError: errorToThrow,
+      afterSessionRan: true,
+    });
   });
 });

